BT 1 0 0 1 30 1320 Tm 3 Tr /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL (The Method at a Glance When someone says \223we want to build an AI agent,\224 there is no TOGAF to reach for, no well-architected framework. This is the) Tj T* (method I use instead: six gates, passed in order. Most agent failures trace back to a skipped gate. I Justify Should this be an agent at all? II Grade) Tj T* (How much can this thing hurt us? III Limit Who is allowed to write what? IV Build The smallest supervised loop that could work V Prove What evidence) Tj T* (buys this thing its freedom? VI Run Who maintains the system that maintains itself? With a preface, a worked example, the paper trail, and the usual) Tj T* (objections at the back. Bhargava P The Six Gates \267 2 / 14) Tj T* ET
 
