BT 1 0 0 1 30 1320 Tm 3 Tr /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL (Preface Why gates Clouds got a well-architected framework. Enterprises got TOGAF. Agents got a demo culture. When the industry is missing a method,) Tj T* (every team improvises one, and improvised methods fail in the same six places: agents that should have been cron jobs, autonomy granted by enthusiasm,) Tj T* (tool access nobody mapped, architectures built for the demo, evidence that amounts to \223we watched it,\224 and systems nobody owns at 2am. So this is not) Tj T* (a framework. It is six questions, asked in a fixed order, each one a gate : you do not proceed until you pass. Any engineer can run them in a one-hour) Tj T* (session with a whiteboard. The order matters, because every gate protects the ones behind it. Read it in ten minutes. Use it on your next agent) Tj T* (request. ) Tj /F2 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\247) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( A method you can hold in your head is the only kind that survives a meeting. Bhargava P The Six Gates \267 3 / 14) Tj T* ET
 
endstream
