BT 1 0 0 1 30 1320 Tm 3 Tr /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL (Gate I of VI Justify Should this be an agent at all? justify  \267  verb  \267  to prove a task needs an agent at all, before any architecture is drawn.) Tj T* (Apply the Rubric Test : can you write down the checklist for judging the output? If yes, build a workflow or a validator, not an agent. Agents earn) Tj T* (their complexity only where judgment is needed at runtime, on inputs you cannot enumerate. To pass, complete the sentence: \223This must be an agent) Tj T* (because the decision cannot be specified in advance, specifically because\205\224 Figure 1. The Rubric Test, applied before any architecture is drawn.) Tj T* (Failure smells like A beautiful agent demo doing a task a cron job could do. ) Tj /F2 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\247) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( If you can write the checklist, build the boring thing. It works.) Tj T* (Bhargava P The Six Gates \267 4 / 14) Tj T* ET
 
