BT 1 0 0 1 30 1320 Tm 3 Tr /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL (Gate IV of VI Build What is the smallest supervised loop that could work? build  \267  verb  \267  to assemble the smallest supervised loop that could do) Tj T* (the job. One agent before multi-agent. Supervised before autonomous: the agent drafts, a human approves, every consequential call passes a checkpoint.) Tj T* (Underneath, a cascade: small models for rubric-writable steps, the frontier model only for judgment, humans for the truly weird. Figure 4. The) Tj T* (supervised loop, and the model cascade underneath it. Failure smells like A five-agent orchestra on day one, fully autonomous, with no human) Tj T* (checkpoint and no logs. ) Tj /F2 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\247) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( The best agent architecture usually invokes the expensive model least. Bhargava P The Six Gates \267 7 / 14) Tj T* ET
 
