BT 1 0 0 1 30 1320 Tm 3 Tr /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL (Gate V of VI Prove What evidence buys this thing its freedom? prove  \267  verb  \267  to purchase autonomy with frozen, reproducible evals instead of) Tj T* (demos. Nothing gets autonomy because it demoed well. Freedom is purchased with evals: a benchmark passed before each promotion, from suggestion-only) Tj T* (to human-approved to autonomous, tool by tool. Freeze the eval before the run. Keep the results. Let anyone reproduce them. And the gate swings both) Tj T* (ways: any change to the model, the prompt, or the tools sends the agent back through it. Figure 5. Promotion is gated by frozen, reproducible evals,) Tj T* (never by demos. Failure smells like \223How do we know it works?\224 answered with \223we watched it for a while.\224 ) Tj /F2 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\247) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( Autonomy is not granted. It is purchased) Tj T* (with evidence. Bhargava P The Six Gates \267 8 / 14) Tj T* ET
 
