BT 1 0 0 1 30 1320 Tm 3 Tr /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL (Gate VI of VI Run Who maintains the system that maintains itself? run  \267  verb  \267  to keep a production agent owned, logged, and pruned, with a name) Tj T* (on the pager. Production agents rot in three places: prompts accrete, tool catalogs sprawl, and self-improving agents now write their own skills. The) Tj T* (cure is a ledger: prompts and skills in version control with owners, provenance notes on anything the agent authors, a scheduled deletion pass,) Tj T* (escalation logs reviewed like gold, and an off switch you have actually tested. Figure 6. The operating ledger. Nothing enters the system without an) Tj T* (owner. Failure smells like A system prompt that has grown for six months and never shrunk once. That is not a prompt. That is a landfill. ) Tj /F2 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\247) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( Give the) Tj T* (agent the pen. Keep the ledger. Bhargava P The Six Gates \267 9 / 14) Tj T* ET
 
