BT 1 0 0 1 30 1320 Tm 3 Tr /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL (A Worked Example One agent, six gates An expense-report triage agent walks the whole path. The request arrives the usual way: \223can we get an AI agent) Tj T* (to handle expense reports?\224 Here is the one-hour session, gate by gate. I Justify Policy limits are a rubric, so they become a validator. The) Tj T* (ambiguous twenty percent, handwritten receipts and split trips, cannot be enumerated. The agent earns its place there only. II Grade It can block) Tj T* (someone\222s reimbursement, which is money-adjacent. Tier 2: it reads everything and decides nothing. It recommends. III Limit approve_or_reject: human) Tj T* (pen. employee_id and amount: application pen. The rationale text: model pen. Enforced in the tool layer, not the prompt. IV Build One agent drafts a) Tj T* (recommendation citing the policy lines it used. A small model sorts receipt types; the frontier model sees only the weird ones. A reviewer approves.) Tj T* (Everything is logged. V Prove Two hundred frozen historical cases. It must beat the checklist baseline before it may auto-approve even the cleanest) Tj T* (category. VI Run Prompt in version control with an owner. Monthly deletion pass. Escalations reviewed weekly. A name, not a team, on the pager. ) Tj /F2 9 Tf 10.8 TL (\247) Tj /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ( Ten) Tj T* (minutes per gate, and the design wrote itself. Bhargava P The Six Gates \267 10 / 14) Tj T* ET
 
endstream
endobj
